 "readme": {
  "overview": "Sitemaps are an easy way for webmasters to inform search engines about the pages on their sites that are available for crawling. In its simplest form, a Sitemap is an XML file that lists URLs for a site along with additional metadata about each URL (when it was last updated, how often it usually changes and how important it is, relative to other URLs in the site) so that search engines could crawl the site more intelligently.",
  "keyFeatures": [
   "Async Sitemap generator",
   "Support big catalogs",
   "Export products and categories",
   "Rich API"
  ],
